flowchart TB
  accTitle: Modern systems cover separate B2 control edges
  accDescr: PALADIN and AgentDebugX contribute failure diagnosis and recovery selection. Shepherd contributes reversible execution traces and branching. AgentHER and Reflexion contribute changes to later behavior from failed experience. Fan and Lan identify the full typed impasse, protected branch, typed return, and condition-safe compilation coupling as still absent from the reviewed systems.
  subgraph D[Diagnosis and recovery]
    P[PALADIN]
    A[AgentDebugX]
  end
  subgraph B[Protected branch]
    S[Shepherd]
  end
  subgraph L[Later behavior change]
    H[AgentHER]
    R[Reflexion]
  end
  D --> PD[Failure-specific recovery selection]
  B --> PB[Reversible fork / replay]
  L --> PL[Cross-episode behavior update]
  PD --> GAP[Residual B2 coupling]
  PB --> GAP
  PL --> GAP
  GAP[Typed impasse + protected substate + typed return + condition-safe compilation]
